+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Electron Security <security@electronjs.org>
+Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:10:09 +0000
+Subject: tls: reject chains containing blocked public keys
+
+Node has no equivalent of Chromium's SPKI blocklist, so a chain through a
+key on that list still verifies in Node as long as it reaches a trusted
+root. Install a certificate verify callback on every SecureContext that
+wraps X509_verify_cert and reports X509_V_ERR_CERT_REVOKED when any
+certificate in the verified chain (or, if no chain could be built, any
+certificate the peer sent) has a SubjectPublicKeyInfo hash on a small
+compiled-in list. The list mirrors the entries Electron adds to Chromium's
+net blocklist. Test-only hooks allow the spec suite to extend the list at
+runtime.
